# Configuration for haos-installer.sh -- the one BUILT INTO the unattended ISO
# (haos-isoinstall-<ref>-unattended-amd64.iso).
#
# This is not the template you are meant to edit; haos-installer.cfg.example is.
# This is the file the unattended image itself runs with, and the two lines at
# the bottom are what make it unattended: no question is asked, and WIPE=yes
# stands in for the typed consent the wizard would otherwise demand. A machine
# booted from that image therefore loses the disk it picks, with no confirmation
# anywhere on screen.
#
# That is the whole point of the variant, and the reason it is a separate
# download from the normal image. The build copies this file to the ISO surface
# too, so it can be read before anything is booted.
#
# DISK is left out on purpose. With one eligible disk the installer takes it;
# with two or more it stops and logs which ones it saw instead of guessing. Add
# DISK=/dev/sda (or /dev/nvme0n1) to choose one, and LANG=/POWEROFF= if wanted:
# every key in haos-installer.cfg.example works here as well.
#
# This file is the weakest of the three layers that can speak, so it is not the
# only way to change them: a haos-installer.cfg on a stick is applied on top of
# it, key by key, and so is anything typed on the kernel command line
# (haos.lang=da haos.poweroff=yes). Rebuilding for one key is never necessary.
UNATTENDED=yes
WIPE=yes
